                <p>I’m interested in the whole system — not just what appears on the screen, but where a request goes, what decides who gets in, and how separate parts become one reliable product.</p>
                <p>That started in high school, when I ran a Minecraft server hosting company for paying customers and learned what breaks when no one is watching. Eight years on a Volvo assembly line showed me the same thing at scale. Today it draws me toward services, integrations, and the infrastructure that connects them.</p>
